            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0599" n="591" xml:id="pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/749: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-12T23:00:00+01:00">September 12, 1938—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 12—6:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>907. Tonight following a meeting of the Prime Minister and principal Ministers to
                    consider Hitler’s speech Cadogan who was present at the meeting gave to a member
                    of the staff the following résumé of what in his opinion the impression of the
                    Ministers had been:</p>
                <p>The speech contained highly offensive expressions which 20 years ago no one would
                    have believed a man holding a position of such responsibility could have made.
                    It does not seem, however, that Hitler has closed the door entirely nor yet put
                    his hand to the trigger. The speech is not obviously as extremely bad as it
                    might have been in spite of its offensive nature and the Ministers were
                    unwilling to reach any final conclusions or decisions tonight. The Cabinet will
                    meet tomorrow afternoon at 3 when more definite views can be formulated.</p>
                <p>The Undersecretary of State did not give the impression that he felt the speech
                    had contributed in any way to relief of existing tension.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
